/* worked example 3: variable specific heat */
{s:2,k:'calc',term:"Worked example 3",title:"Worked example 3: variable specific heat",say:'Same heat as the Otto example, but now the specific heat grows with temperature. Integrate it, and you get a quadratic in T three. Solve it: fifteen hundred fifty-three kelvin.',cues:{fk:'Same heat as',k1:'Integrate it',k1b:'a quadratic in',k2:'Solve it',k2b:'fifteen hundred fifty-three'},q:['The Otto example again: qin = 797.5 kJ/kg, T₂ = 689.2 K, p₂ = 18.38 bar.','Now cv = 0.71 + 0.00019 T kJ/kg·K. Find the new peak T₃ and p₃.'],f:['qin = ∫ cv dT, from T₂ to T₃','= 0.71 (T₃ − T₂) + 0.000095 (T₃² − T₂²)','p₃ = p₂ T₃ / T₂ (constant volume)'],hint:'Solve the quadratic for T₃.',fk:'fk',steps:[["Set up", ["797.5 = 0.71 (T₃ − 689.2) + 0.000095 (T₃² − 475 000)", "0.000095 T₃² + 0.71 T₃ − 1332.0 = 0"], ["k1","k1b"]], ["Solve", ["T₃ = (−0.71 + 1.0051) / 0.00019", "T₃ = 1553 K"], ["k2","k2b"]], ["Peak pressure", ["p₃ = 18.38 × 1553 / 689.2", "p₃ = 41.4 bar"], ["k3","k3b"]], ["Against constant cv", ["1800 − 1553 = 247 K cooler", "247 K cooler, 6.6 bar lower than 48.0 bar"], ["k4","k4b"]]],live:[0,1]},
{s:2,k:'calc',term:"Worked example 3 (pressure)",title:"Worked example 3: variable specific heat",say:'At constant volume, the peak pressure is forty-one point four bar. That is two hundred forty-seven kelvin cooler, and six point six bar lower, than with constant specific heat.',pause:1.0,cues:{fk:'At constant volume',k3:'the peak pressure',k3b:'forty-one point',k4:'That is two',k4b:'six point six',a:'than with constant'},q:['The Otto example again: qin = 797.5 kJ/kg, T₂ = 689.2 K, p₂ = 18.38 bar.','Now cv = 0.71 + 0.00019 T kJ/kg·K. Find the new peak T₃ and p₃.'],f:['qin = ∫ cv dT, from T₂ to T₃','= 0.71 (T₃ − T₂) + 0.000095 (T₃² − T₂²)','p₃ = p₂ T₃ / T₂ (constant volume)'],hint:'Solve the quadratic for T₃.',fk:'fk',steps:[["Set up", ["797.5 = 0.71 (T₃ − 689.2) + 0.000095 (T₃² − 475 000)", "0.000095 T₃² + 0.71 T₃ − 1332.0 = 0"], ["k1","k1b"]], ["Solve", ["T₃ = (−0.71 + 1.0051) / 0.00019", "T₃ = 1553 K"], ["k2","k2b"]], ["Peak pressure", ["p₃ = 18.38 × 1553 / 689.2", "p₃ = 41.4 bar"], ["k3","k3b"]], ["Against constant cv", ["1800 − 1553 = 247 K cooler", "247 K cooler, 6.6 bar lower than 48.0 bar"], ["k4","k4b"]]],live:[2,3],ans:['T₃ = 1553 K, p₃ = 41.4 bar','a']},
/* worked example 4: indicator diagram and efficiencies */
{s:2,k:'calc',term:"Worked example 4",title:"Worked example 4: from the indicator diagram",say:`Subtract the pumping loop: three hundred sixty-two joules. Over five hundred cubic centimeters, the indicated ${P('mep')} is seven point two four bar. The fuel brings eleven hundred twenty-two joules a cycle.`,cues:{fk:'Subtract the pumping',k1:'Subtract the pumping',k1b:'three hundred sixty-two',k2:'Over five hundred',k2b:'seven point two',k3:'The fuel brings',k3b:'eleven hundred'},q:['Four-stroke, Vs = 500 cm³, 3000 rev/min: main loop 380 J, pumping loop 18 J.','Brake work 290 J, fuel 0.0255 g at 44 MJ/kg, per cycle. Find imep, ηi, ηm, ηb, friction power.'],f:['Wi = main loop − pumping loop','imep = Wi / Vs','ηi = Wi / Qf,  ηm = Wb / Wi,  ηb = ηi ηm','cycles per second = N / 120'],hint:'Four-stroke: one cycle every two revolutions.',fk:'fk',steps:[["Net indicated work", ["Wi = 380 − 18", "Wi = 362 J"], ["k1","k1b"]], ["Indicated mep", ["362 / (500 × 10⁻⁶ m³)", "imep = 724 000 Pa = 7.24 bar"], ["k2","k2b"]], ["Fuel energy per cycle", ["Qf = 0.0255 × 10⁻³ kg × 44 × 10⁶ J/kg", "Qf = 1122 J"], ["k3","k3b"]], ["Efficiencies", ["362 / 1122,  290 / 362,  290 / 1122", "ηi = 32.3 %, ηm = 80.1 %, ηb = 25.8 %"], ["k4","k4b"]], ["Friction power", ["(362 − 290) J × 25 per s", "friction power = 1.80 kW"], ["k5","k5b"]]],live:[0,1,2]},
{s:2,k:'calc',term:"Worked example 4 (efficiencies)",title:"Worked example 4: from the indicator diagram",say:'Indicated efficiency, thirty-two point three percent. Mechanical, eighty point one. Brake, twenty-five point eight. At twenty-five cycles a second, friction eats one point eight kilowatts.',pause:1.0,cues:{fk:'Indicated efficiency',k4:'Indicated efficiency',k4b:'Brake, twenty-five',k5:'At twenty-five',k5b:'friction eats',a:'one point eight'},q:['Four-stroke, Vs = 500 cm³, 3000 rev/min: main loop 380 J, pumping loop 18 J.','Brake work 290 J, fuel 0.0255 g at 44 MJ/kg, per cycle. Find imep, ηi, ηm, ηb, friction power.'],f:['Wi = main loop − pumping loop','imep = Wi / Vs','ηi = Wi / Qf,  ηm = Wb / Wi,  ηb = ηi ηm','cycles per second = N / 120'],hint:'Four-stroke: one cycle every two revolutions.',fk:'fk',steps:[["Net indicated work", ["Wi = 380 − 18", "Wi = 362 J"], ["k1","k1b"]], ["Indicated mep", ["362 / (500 × 10⁻⁶ m³)", "imep = 724 000 Pa = 7.24 bar"], ["k2","k2b"]], ["Fuel energy per cycle", ["Qf = 0.0255 × 10⁻³ kg × 44 × 10⁶ J/kg", "Qf = 1122 J"], ["k3","k3b"]], ["Efficiencies", ["362 / 1122,  290 / 362,  290 / 1122", "ηi = 32.3 %, ηm = 80.1 %, ηb = 25.8 %"], ["k4","k4b"]], ["Friction power", ["(362 − 290) J × 25 per s", "friction power = 1.80 kW"], ["k5","k5b"]]],live:[3,4],ans:['imep 7.24 bar, ηb 25.8 %, friction 1.80 kW','a']},
{s:2,k:'trap2',term:'Exam trap',title:'Exam trap!',say:'Exam trap. Never write that variable specific heat raises the peak. Write that it lowers it: the same heat, a bigger specific heat, a smaller temperature rise.',cues:{x:'Exam trap',w:'Never write that',r:'Write that it'},wl:"Don't write",rl:'Write',wrong:['Variable specific heat raises','the peak temperature.'],right:['cv rises, so ΔT = q / cv falls:','T₃ = 1553 K, not 1800 K.'],wv:(c,u,b)=>
 Q4_bars([['constant cv',1800,'#ADB5BD'],['variable cv',2000,'#CED4DA']],170,290,230,2000,110,80,()=>'')+Q4_T(445,48,'higher?',{fs:28,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:TRED})+Q4_arrow(530,150,530,70,TRED,5),
 rv:(c,u,b)=>
 Q4_bars([['constant cv',1800,'#ADB5BD'],['variable cv',1553,GRN]],140,286,230,2000,110,80,Q4_K)+Q4_T(560,170,'247 K',{fs:28,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:GRN})+Q4_T(560,202,'lower',{fs:24,fw:700,a:'middle',fill:GRN})+Q4_L(470,(286-1800/2000*230).toFixed(1),470,(286-1553/2000*230).toFixed(1),GRN,4)},
/* ---- recap ---- */
{s:RC,k:'recap',term:'Recap',say:'Recap in three. Same compression ratio, Otto wins; same peak pressure, Diesel wins. Real gas lowers the peak: about four fifths of the ideal efficiency. And the indicator diagram shows each loss, before friction takes its share.',cues:{r1:'Same compression ratio',r2:'Real gas lowers',r3:'And the indicator'},panels:[["Which cycle wins","BLU",'q4Rank',['Same r: Otto > dual > Diesel.','Same peak p: Diesel > dual > Otto.'],'r1'],["Real gas","ORG",'q4Gas',['Variable cv, dissociation:','peak 1553 K, not 1800 K.'],'r2'],["Indicator diagram","GRN",'q4Ind',['Wi = main loop − pumping loop.','ηb = ηi × ηm.'],'r3']],live:[0,1,2]},
/* ---- exam practice ---- */
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"Why is the spark advanced before TDC?",say:'Question one. Why is the spark fired before top dead center?',cues:{k:'Question one',q:'Why is the'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"Why is the spark advanced before TDC?",say:'Burning takes forty to sixty degrees of crank angle. Starting it early centers the pressure rise near top dead center, and keeps the time loss small.',cues:{a1:'Burning takes forty',a2:'Starting it early'},al:[["Burning takes 40° to 60° of crank angle.",'a1'],["Starting early centres the pressure rise near TDC: least time loss.",'a2']],vis:(c,u,b)=>{
 const cx=310,cy=245,R=155,pt=d=>{const a=(d-90)*Math.PI/180;return [(cx+R*Math.cos(a)).toFixed(1),(cy+R*Math.sin(a)).toFixed(1)]};
 const [x0,y0]=pt(-25),[x1,y1]=pt(25);
 let s=`<circle cx="${cx}" cy="${cy}" r="${R}" fill="none" stroke="#ADB5BD" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="10 8"/>`+Q4_L(cx,cy,cx,cy-R,Q4_STEEL,10)+`<circle cx="${cx}" cy="${cy}" r="16" fill="#343A40"/>`+
  Q4_T(cx,cy-R-24,'TDC',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle'})+Q4_T(cx,cy+R+40,'BDC',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:Q4_GREY})+Q4_arrow(cx+R*0.70,cy+R*0.72,cx+R*0.95,cy+R*0.30,Q4_GREY,4)+Q4_T(cx+R+20,cy+R*0.62,'crank turns',{fs:22,fill:Q4_GREY});
 s+=g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),`<path d="M${x0},${y0} A${R},${R} 0 0 1 ${x1},${y1}" fill="none" stroke="${ORG}" stroke-width="16" stroke-linecap="round"/>`+`<circle cx="${x0}" cy="${y0}" r="12" fill="${GRN}"/>`+Q4_T(x0-20,y0+6,'spark',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'end',fill:GRN})+Q4_T(cx,cy+60,'burning:',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:ORG})+Q4_T(cx,cy+92,'40° to 60° of crank',{fs:22,fw:700,a:'middle',fill:ORG}));
 s+=g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),`<circle cx="${cx}" cy="${cy-R}" r="16" fill="${BLU}"/>`+Q4_T(cx+40,cy-R-50,'pressure rise',{fs:22,fw:800,fill:BLU})+Q4_T(cx+40,cy-R-24,'centred near TDC',{fs:22,fw:700,fill:BLU})+Q4_box(140,462,340,44,{fill:'#E7F5FF',st:BLU,sw:2,r:22})+Q4_T(310,492,'least time loss',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:BLU}));
 return s}},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"An Otto cycle has r = 10 and γ = 1.4. Find its efficiency.",say:`Question two. An ${P('Otto')} cycle has a compression ratio of ten, and gamma one point four. Find its efficiency.`,cues:{k:'Question two',q:'cycle has a'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"An Otto cycle has r = 10 and γ = 1.4. Find its efficiency.",say:'Ten to the power zero point four is two point five one two. One over that is zero point three nine eight. So the efficiency is sixty point two percent.',cues:{fk:'Ten to the',k1:'Ten to the',k1b:'two point five',k2:'One over that',k2b:'zero point three',k3:'So the efficiency',k3b:'sixty point two'},calc:{f:[`η = 1 − 1 / ${Q4_sup('r','γ−1')}`],hint:'γ − 1 = 0.4',fk:'fk',steps:[["Power",[`${Q4_sup('10','0.4')}`,`${Q4_sup('10','0.4')} = 2.512`],["k1","k1b"]],["Reciprocal",["1 / 2.512","1 / 2.512 = 0.398"],["k2","k2b"]],["Efficiency",["η = 1 − 0.398","η = 0.602 = 60.2 %"],["k3","k3b"]]],live:[0,1,2]}},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"Rank the Otto, dual and Diesel cycles for the same r and heat input, and for the same peak pressure and heat input. Explain the reversal.",say:`Question three. Rank the ${P('Otto')}, dual and Diesel cycles for the same compression ratio and heat input, then for the same peak pressure and heat input. Explain the reversal.`,cues:{k:'Question three',q:'Rank the'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"Rank the Otto, dual and Diesel cycles for the same r and heat input, and for the same peak pressure and heat input. Explain the reversal.",say:`Same compression ratio: ${P('Otto')}, dual, then Diesel, because Otto adds all its heat at the smallest volume. Same peak pressure: the order flips. The limit lets Diesel run a much higher ratio, so it rejects less heat.`,cues:{a1:'Same compression ratio',a2:'Same peak pressure'},al:[["Same r: Otto > dual > Diesel; Otto adds all its heat at the smallest volume.",'a1'],["Same peak p: Diesel > dual > Otto; the limit lets Diesel run a much higher r, so it rejects less heat.",'a2']],vis:(c,u,b)=>{
 const row=(y,title,names,cols)=>Q4_T(310,y,title,{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle'})+[[0,140],[1,95],[2,60]].map(([i,h],j)=>{const x=60+j*175,base=y+200,rank=j+1;return `<rect x="${x}" y="${base-h}" width="150" height="${h}" rx="6" fill="${cols[i]}"/>`+Q4_T(x+75,base-h+38,String(rank),{fs:30,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:'#FFFFFF'})+Q4_T(x+75,base-h-12,names[i],{fs:22,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:cols[i]})}).join('')+Q4_L(40,y+200,580,y+200,Q4_GREY,3);
 return g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),row(30,'same r and heat input',['Otto','dual','Diesel'],[BLU,PUR,'#868E96']))+g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),row(270,'same peak pressure and heat input',['Diesel','dual','Otto'],[GRN,PUR,'#868E96']))}},
{s:LS,k:'figs',term:'Your notes',title:'For your notes',say:'Your free notes are the PDF in the description. Redraw both pressure-volume diagrams, then check every number.',cues:{t:'Your free notes',f:'Redraw both'},tags:[["Free notes for this lesson (PDF)", "link in the description"], ["The two chapters", "Ideal air-standard cycles and their comparison; Fuel-air cycles and actual cycle analysis"], ["Key terms and glossary", "at the end of the notes"]],figs:[["Otto and Diesel to scale", "From 1 bar and 300 K both peak near 48 bar; the Diesel loop (r = 16) encloses 561 kJ/kg against the Otto cycle’s 450 kJ/kg (r = 8)."], ["Indicator diagram over the Otto cycle", "Time loss rounds the top, wall heat loss lowers expansion, early exhaust opening cuts the BDC corner, and the pumping loop is negative work: 380 J main loop, 18 J pumping loop."]],note:"Sources your free notes draw on: John B. Heywood (Internal Combustion Engine Fundamentals); V. Ganesan (Internal Combustion Engines)"},
{s:OUT,k:'outro',term:'Outro',say:'So remember: say what is held equal, real gas lowers the peak, and subtract the pumping loop. Next time, carburetors and their mixture circuits. See you there!',cues:{f:'So remember',w1:'say what is',w2:'real gas lowers',w3:'and subtract the',n:'Next time',s:'See you there'},words:[['SAY WHAT IS HELD EQUAL','BLU','w1'],['REAL GAS: A LOWER PEAK','ORG','w2'],['Wi = MAIN − PUMPING LOOP','GRN','w3']],next:["NEXT TIME", "Next lesson", "Carburettors: mixture requirements and circuits", "book"],end:'See you there!'}
